hitler wrote:
>
> I read a post on here about two months ago, where the punchline was
> something like "Woe be unto he who does not suffer his pet to live."

Most people with high ascension percentages take this stance.  It is
best to consider any advice from people that skilled.

> Not having a pet will garner more early experience for a character
> because all kills will be made by character.

There are monsters in abundance in the mines.  Pay attention to what
monsters you kill and what monsters the pet kills - You may learn a very
good strategy.  There's more to it than just killing the peacefuls for
you.  But killing the peacefuls for you is a very good use of pets.

> Pet is just gonna die on level 3 anyway, so keeping it would just be
> Wasted Time.

I lose some pets to traps in the early game but I lose most of them far
deeper than that.  It doesn't take much attention to keep them alive.

> Many creatures in the dungeon can be tamed, so perhaps one should wait
> until the desired unicorn is within a red gem's throw.

Certainly it is not the end of the world to lose a pet.

> And the one that is my main reason for not keeping pet: Countless
> complexity is added to my maneuvering in stepping over the goddamn
> thing.

In exchange for killing the popcorn monsters that are no longer worth
your while pets do at least these services:

1) Tell you which items are cursed.

2) Rob shops for you.

3) Block one direction in corridors as you travel.

4) Fight monsters than you don't want to fight yourself.

The first two reasons become less useful as you get deeper.  The last
one takes an extremely powerful pet.  This suggests that pets are more
valuable in the early game than in the mid game and more valuable in the
end game than in the late game.  Their value is not constant throughout
the game.

> Additionally, since I kill anything that moves except for a
> rare peaceful creature, moving pet keeps firing off false red alerts
> in my vision.

That's an invalid reason.  Have your pet hilighted.

> If I see one counterpoint to what I have written, I will be feeled
> with a red confusing monster glow.

I have left pets in mine town after coming back up.  A pet who can kill
the mine town watch captain can get me a very good weapon, but it can
also kill shopkeepers and then attack and get killed by the mine town
priest ...


